Dear phishing@pot,


I was reviewing renewal records this week and wanted to reach out personall=
y about your certification(s), since your current cycle is coming up on its=
 deadline.=20

Here's where things stand: your logged ECE credits are currently below the =
120 required for this cycle, and your CE fee has been overdue 2 year(s). I =
wanted you to hear this from me directly rather than through an automated e=
mail. You've put real work into earning the certification(s), and we don't =
want to see you lose it over something fixable.=20

On the ECE credits side, you may be closer than you think. A wide range of =
activities qualify, including training, webinars, conferences, item writing=
, and volunteering. Many members find they've already done things that coun=
t but just haven't logged them yet. It's worth taking a few minutes in your=
 Aspen account to review and submit anything recent.=20

There's also something that should make closing the gap much easier. Once y=
our CE dues are current, you'll receive a complimentary 1-year subscription=
 to EC-Council's Learning Library (worth $399), that's 120+ microlearning c=
ybersecurity courses you can use to stay sharp and earn credits toward your=
 requirement. To claim it, just write to support@eccouncil.org <mailto:supp=
ort@eccouncil.org>  after your payment and our team will activate your acce=
ss.=20

