                  </p>
=20
                  <p>
                    Here's where things stand: your logged ECE credits are =
currently below the 120 required for this cycle, and your CE fee has been o=
verdue 2 year(s). I wanted you to hear this from me directly rather than th=
rough an automated email. You've put real work into earning the certificati=
on(s), and we don't want to see you lose it over something fixable.
                  </p>
=20
                  <p>
                    On the ECE credits side, you may be closer than you thi=
nk. A wide range of activities qualify, including training, webinars, confe=
rences, item writing, and volunteering. Many members find they've already d=
one things that count but just haven't logged them yet. It's worth taking a=
 few minutes in your Aspen account to review and submit anything recent.
                  </p>
=20
                  <p>
                    There's also something that should make closing the gap=
 much easier. Once your CE dues are current, you'll receive a <strong>compl=
imentary 1-year subscription to EC-Council's Learning Library</strong> (wor=
th $399), that's 120+ microlearning cybersecurity courses you can use to st=
ay sharp and earn credits toward your requirement. To claim it, just write =
to <a href=3D"mailto:support@eccouncil.org" style=3D"color:#b00020;">suppor=
t@eccouncil.org</a> after your payment and our team will activate your acce=
ss.
                  </p>
